lda shows up during the  final battle fighting right alongside  linking Ganondorf serenity the cult  series Firefly enjoyed a second life  through the movie serenity and now ready  player one marks the second film  appearance of the series iconic ship  serenity or at least some kind of fire  fight class spaceship it first appears  outside the destructed globe the dance  club planet where Wade and Artemis meet  up the second appearance of serenity  comes closer to the end of the film when  it soars out over the battle and then  Taito leaps from his loading bay to join  the war on planet doom we still would  have liked to see Captain Mal  but we'll take what we can get Star  Tribune Spielberg apparently spent years  getting the rights to use Star Wars  characters and ready player one and  after all that work references to the  sci-fi juggernaut are still incredibly  hard to spot so if you look very  carefully you'll see a couple of you'll  see an r2d2 somewhere you'll see an  x-wing somewhere the wall Star Wars got  a few cartoon odds Star Trek got an  entire scene recreation well more or  less the scene in question appears when  holidays death is first announced and he  releases his Easter Egg video to the  world at the very beginning of that  video he's seen lying in a coffin  reminiscent of Sparks coffin in Star  Trek 2 the Wrath of Khan  the Starfleet insignia is even visible  as a flower wreath to draw in the scene  sneaking it past Spielberg despite all  the references to Spielberg's films in  the book the director was keen to leave  those out of the ready player one movie  because he didn't want the whole thing  to become too self referential aside  from some Back to the Future gags and  the t-rex there are no spielberg  sanctioned spielberg easter eggs in the  movie but that didn't stop the  production team they just had to get  even more creative  for example somewhere in with all those  characters in the final oasis battle  supposedly there's one little gremlin  fighting in the mix no III didn't even  notice a gremlin show a couple of times  that I had been working on the effect  shots and I remember after about four  times seeing the same shot I said who  snuck a gremlin in this Zemeckis cube  Spielberg may have clamped down on  references to many of his films but back  to the future sure got a lot of love and  ready player one that the Lorien that  way drives in the Oasis is a most  obvious example and there was this line  I'll wave to you from the finish line  McFly but there were several more  obscure Easter eggs from the franchise  hidden throughout the film inside h's  Oasis workshop eagle-eyed viewers can  spot a hoverboard from Back to the  Future 2 but the best one has got to go  to the Zemeckis cube the magical  artifact Wade buys in the mall after  finding the first key the name of course  is a reference to Robert Zemeckis who  directed all three Back to the Future  films but this cease to rag went another  layer deeper when it turned out that the  Zemeckis cube had the power to turn back  time Jack Slater 3 according to a  theater marquee the cars passing the big  race scene at the beginning of the movie  Arnold Schwarzenegger was starring in a  movie called Jack Slater 3 if that name  sounds vaguely familiar there's a reason  for it in the 1993 movie Last Action  Hero Arnold Schwarzenegger stars as  Chuck Slater a character in a cheesy  action film franchise that exists only  within the movie you think you're funny  don't you  I know I am and the famous comedian and  Tiger to some title the movie playing at  the beginning of the Last Action Hero is  you guessed it Jack Slater 3 meltdown  the Iron Giant was a fantastic addition  to ready player one his appearance alone  isn't an easter egg obviously but he did  get one good Easter again after helping  the crew reach Castle anorak hni and  Jane fall down and sink into a pool of  lava but just before the metal man is  gone for good he gives them all the  thumbs-up it's a recreation of the scene  in Terminator 2 Judgment Day where  Arnie's t800 shoots John and Sarah  Connor a thumbs up as he sinks into a  vat of molten metal Mad Bulls if you  spent any amount of time alive in the  80s you probably had a mud ball if you  miss him the first time around  Mad Bulls were these rubber balls with  the monster faces that was about it so  don't worry you didn't miss out on much  during one scene artemis grabbed a  living man pool and used as a grenade  but the things were all over the rest of  the movie - there's a detailed mud ball  painted on one of the trainers and the  stacks and this behind the scenes  article from Entertainment Weekly shows  another one painted on the walls of  Artemis's rebellion headquarters weapon  cameos marbles weren't the only weird  weapons and ready player one one of the  items are Wade picks up in the Oasis  mall is the Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch  we  you may recognize from Monty Python and  the Holy Grail he later uses the Holy  Hand Grenade during the battle although  it doesn't even count to three before  throwing it there were plenty of other  weapon cameos as well for an instant you  can see a Star Trek about laughs in one  scene and in the ending battle Wade  whips out a halo rocket launcher which  he fires at the sixer army from a  speeding DeLorean Deadeye part a army of  Darkness is dead I'd say everywhere in  the battle scenes of ready player one in  the same theme of chun-li and tracer you  can spot a handful of them this clip of  halo Spartans charging into battle yup  it Deadites there too granted they're  probably an easy model to use for  filling out those massive battle shots  just repeats some sword wielding  skeletons a few dozen times and you have  yourself an army but in the movie  universe you have to wonder why there  would be so many Deadites remember each  of those characters is ostensibly a real  person who chose up form to play in the  Oasis the only explanation is that 